WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:07.899 --> 00:00:13.901
We were in a store. and a guy in that
store told us to put our uniforms on.

2
00:00:14.071 --> 00:00:17.238
“What the hell are you talking about?”

3
00:00:17.407 --> 00:00:22.034
He says. “The U.S.A's
in a war with Japan.”

4
00:00:22.203 --> 00:00:23.745
We couldn't believe it.

5
00:00:23.913 --> 00:00:26.949
Our country was attacked.
It's a different—

6
00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:31.453
It wasn't like Korea or Vietnam.
We was attacked.

7
00:00:31.629 --> 00:00:34.748
And. you know. it was a feeling of…

8
00:00:34.923 --> 00:00:38.920
Maybe we're just dumb country
people where I come from…

9
00:00:39.094 --> 00:00:41.252
but a lot of us volunteered.

10
00:00:41.429 --> 00:00:46.137
“Who would like to volunteer
for the Tank Corps? For the Air Force?

11
00:00:46.308 --> 00:00:49.475
For the Navy?” Or whatever.

12
00:00:49.645 --> 00:00:53.689
Then they said. “Who would
volunteer for the Airborne?”

13
00:00:53.857 --> 00:00:56.810
So I says.
“What the hell's the Airborne?”

14
00:00:56.985 --> 00:00:59.558
We came from a small. small town…

15
00:00:59.737 --> 00:01:05.193
and three fellows in that town
that were 4-F committed suicide.

16
00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:09.364
Because they couldn't go.
A different time.

17
00:01:09.537 --> 00:01:13.238
I did things. I didn't do them
for medals or accolades.

18
00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:17.544
I did them because they…
It's what had to be done.

19
00:01:17.711 --> 00:01:23.831
The guy says. “You jump out
of airplanes to fight the enemy.”

20
00:01:24.009 --> 00:01:27.840
These guys said. “Go to hell.”
Nobody put up their hands.

21
00:01:28.012 --> 00:01:30.633
And I don't know
what brought it up…

22
00:01:30.848 --> 00:01:35.426
but the guy speaking said.
“You get paid $50 a month more.”

23
00:01:35.602 --> 00:01:37.891
So that made it 100 bucks.

24
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:45.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

25
00:04:38.224 --> 00:04:41.427
Okay. boys. let's get
this gear stowed.

26
00:05:01.286 --> 00:05:05.200
Fox Company. we go in five.

27
00:05:08.251 --> 00:05:10.576
–Sergeant Maynard?
–Nope.

28
00:05:12.922 --> 00:05:15.430
In the name of the Father
and the Son…

29
00:05:21.804 --> 00:05:24.426
1st Platoon. draw small arms.

30
00:05:24.599 --> 00:05:27.516
It'll be too late when
you face the enemy.

31
00:05:27.685 --> 00:05:29.807
Easy Company!

32
00:05:30.062 --> 00:05:33.062
Listen up! Gather up around me!

33
00:05:33.231 --> 00:05:34.939
Move it up! Come on!

34
00:05:35.817 --> 00:05:37.477
Let's go!

35
00:05:40.738 --> 00:05:44.071
The Channel coast is socked in
with rain and fog.

36
00:05:44.366 --> 00:05:49.075
High winds on the drop zone.
No jump tonight.

37
00:05:49.246 --> 00:05:53.991
The invasion has been postponed.
We're on a 24-hour stand-down.

38
00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:58.081
–Drill sergeants. take charge.
–1st Platoon…

39
00:05:58.254 --> 00:06:01.504
Well. this is quite a surprise.

40
00:06:01.799 --> 00:06:05.630
Not particularly. It so happens
I rather expected it.

41
00:06:05.802 --> 00:06:11.472
Well. I can't see how you people
can pass up $80·000 for the cause.

42
00:06:11.641 --> 00:06:13.467
For whose cause?

43
00:06:13.642 --> 00:06:18.683
If you're so interested in serving
a cause. why don't you join the Army?

44
00:06:21.107 --> 00:06:23.432
–I'm 4-F.
–You look 1-A to me.

45
00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.147
You don't look so bad yourself.

46
00:06:28.823 --> 00:06:31.230
Well. it's my arteries.

47
00:06:31.408 --> 00:06:33.780
Should you be giving blood?

48
00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:43.075
I think it's clearing up.

49
00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.121
Think it's clearing up?

50
00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.216
Nope.

51
00:06:51.385 --> 00:06:53.543
I think it's clearing up.

52
00:06:55.763 --> 00:06:59.761
–How are your men?
–They'll be fine.

53
00:07:05.314 --> 00:07:10.604
Five o'clock in New York.
Four o'clock in Chicago.

54
00:07:10.777 --> 00:07:14.988
–Happy hour. huh?
–Yeah. happy hour.

55
00:07:15.323 --> 00:07:20.067
A couple of drinks. Maybe
an early dinner before the theater.

56
00:07:26.249 --> 00:07:29.582
Civilized place for civilized men.

57
00:07:33.839 --> 00:07:36.875
Should have been born earlier. Nix.

58
00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:39.623
What. and give up all this?

59
00:07:53.607 --> 00:07:56.524
We'll go to Chicago.
I'll take you there.

60
00:07:56.776 --> 00:07:58.105
Yeah.

61
00:07:59.404 --> 00:08:00.981
We'll see.

62
00:08:09.663 --> 00:08:14.123
–Actually. you know who's from there?
–Who? Oh. him.

63
00:08:15.168 --> 00:08:19.628
712 days with that son of a bitch
and here we are.

64
00:08:45.236 --> 00:08:49.732
You people are at the position
of attention!

65
00:08:56.788 --> 00:09:01.284
Pvt. Perconte. did you blouse
your trousers like a paratrooper?

66
00:09:01.459 --> 00:09:04.662
–No. sir.
–Then explain the creases.

67
00:09:04.837 --> 00:09:07.921
–No excuse. sir.
–Volunteering is one thing.

68
00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:11.091
You've got a long way
to prove you belong.

69
00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:13.964
Your weekend pass is revoked.

70
00:09:14.137 --> 00:09:16.379
–Name.
–Luz. George.

71
00:09:17.807 --> 00:09:21.507
Dirt in the rear sight aperture.
Pass revoked.

72
00:09:33.446 --> 00:09:35.735
When did you sew on the chevron?

73
00:09:35.907 --> 00:09:37.531
Yesterday. sir.

74
00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:40.191
Long enough to notice this. Revoked.

75
00:09:40.369 --> 00:09:41.780
Sir.

76
00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.952
–Name.
–Malarkey. Donald G.

77
00:09:46.124 --> 00:09:50.335
–Isn't “malarkey” slang for bullshit?
–Yes. sir.

78
00:09:51.212 --> 00:09:56.004
Rust on the butt plate hinge spring.
Pvt. Bullshit. Revoked.

79
00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:00.050
–Name.
–Liebgott. Joseph D. sir.

80
00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:05.964
Rusty bayonet. Liebgott.
You wanna kill Germans?

81
00:10:06.142 --> 00:10:08.763
–Yes. sir.
–Not with this.

82
00:10:10.271 --> 00:10:13.722
I wouldn't take this rusty piece
of shit to war…

83
00:10:13.899 --> 00:10:17.065
and I will not take you
in your condition.

84
00:10:17.235 --> 00:10:20.935
Thanks to these men
and their infractions. every man…

85
00:10:21.114 --> 00:10:25.277
who had a weekend pass
has lost it.

86
00:10:27.036 --> 00:10:30.653
Change into your PT gear.
We're running Currahee.

87
00:10:33.166 --> 00:10:36.748
2nd Platoon. fall out.
We have two minutes.

88
00:10:42.007 --> 00:10:44.296
I ain't going up that hill.

89
00:10:44.927 --> 00:10:48.710
Perconte. what are you thinking of.
blousing your pants?

90
00:10:48.888 --> 00:10:53.680
–Shut up. He gigged everybody.
–Don't give him no excuses.

91
00:10:53.851 --> 00:10:58.892
Excuses? Look at these trousers and
tell me if there's a crease on them.

92
00:10:59.064 --> 00:11:02.647
Let's go. On the road.
in PT formation. Let's move.

93
00:11:03.652 --> 00:11:06.652
Perconte. Let's go. Perconte.

94
00:11:09.699 --> 00:11:12.984
Pvt. White. why are you not
in your PT gear?

95
00:11:17.414 --> 00:11:20.201
I asked you a question. private.

96
00:11:37.182 --> 00:11:41.808
Easy Company. While you run.
we'll take your dames to the movies.

97
00:11:41.978 --> 00:11:45.560
Good. they need some female company.

98
00:11:50.318 --> 00:11:52.690
–Where do we run?
–Currahee!

99
00:11:52.862 --> 00:11:55.568
–What's Currahee mean?
–“We stand alone!”

100
00:11:55.656 --> 00:11:59.405
–How far up? How far down?
–Three miles up. three down!

101
00:11:59.577 --> 00:12:02.198
–What company is this?
–Easy Company!

102
00:12:02.371 --> 00:12:04.696
–And what do we do?
–Stand alone!

103
00:12:04.873 --> 00:12:10.163
Do not help that man!
Do not help that man! Do not stop!

104
00:12:11.379 --> 00:12:15.293
You have 13 minutes to get
to the top of this mountain…

105
00:12:15.466 --> 00:12:21.219
if you want to serve
in the paratroopers. Hi-yo. Silver!

106
00:12:46.243 --> 00:12:48.070
Come on. You can make it.

107
00:12:48.245 --> 00:12:51.875
Come on. Alley. Come on. Guarnere.
You got it! Come on!

108
00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.409
Never thought I'd see the day.
Private Wynn.

109
00:12:55.585 --> 00:12:58.502
We are coming on 23 minutes.

110
00:12:58.671 --> 00:13:02.040
That may be good enough
for the rest of the 506…

111
00:13:02.216 --> 00:13:06.047
but that is not good
enough for Easy Company!

112
00:13:15.937 --> 00:13:18.012
We can do this! Come on!

113
00:13:19.606 --> 00:13:21.017
Come on.

114
00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.734
Come on.

115
00:13:46.881 --> 00:13:49.004
I'm gonna say something.

116
00:13:49.175 --> 00:13:50.669
To who?

117
00:13:53.845 --> 00:13:55.672
Lt Winters.

118
00:13:56.181 --> 00:13:59.217
–What is it?
–Permission to speak. sir.

119
00:13:59.601 --> 00:14:03.514
–Permission granted.
–Sir. we've got nine companies. sir.

120
00:14:03.688 --> 00:14:05.063
We do.

121
00:14:05.856 --> 00:14:12.024
Why are we the only one marching every
Friday. 12 miles. in the pitch dark?

122
00:14:12.195 --> 00:14:17.699
–Why do you think. Pvt. Randleman?
–Lt Sobel hates us. sir.

123
00:14:21.787 --> 00:14:25.998
Lt Sobel does not hate Easy Company.
Pvt. Randleman.

124
00:14:26.583 --> 00:14:28.457
He just hates you.

125
00:14:28.918 --> 00:14:30.911
Thank you. sir.

126
00:14:33.297 --> 00:14:36.748
–He hates him back.
–He hates you too. Muck.

127
00:14:36.926 --> 00:14:40.377
Lt Winters. I want canteens out.
caps unscrewed.

128
00:14:40.554 --> 00:14:42.546
Canteens out and open.

129
00:14:42.722 --> 00:14:45.806
They will pour the contents
onto the ground.

130
00:14:45.975 --> 00:14:48.264
You will upend your canteen.

131
00:14:48.436 --> 00:14:51.306
–Now. lieutenant.
–Pour them!

132
00:14:57.069 --> 00:14:58.693
Who is this?

133
00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:02.521
Christenson! Why is there
no water in your canteen?

134
00:15:02.699 --> 00:15:04.691
You drank from your canteen?

135
00:15:04.867 --> 00:15:06.527
–Lt Winters!
–Yes. sir.

136
00:15:06.702 --> 00:15:11.280
Was this man ordered
to not drink from his canteen?

137
00:15:11.456 --> 00:15:14.706
–He was. sir.
–You disobeyed a direct order.

138
00:15:14.876 --> 00:15:19.668
You will fill your canteen
and repeat all 12 miles of the march.

139
00:15:19.839 --> 00:15:22.412
–Yes. sir.
–Fall out!

140
00:15:30.765 --> 00:15:33.849
What are you doing
with my company?

141
00:15:34.018 --> 00:15:37.850
You're late and you allow troopers
to disobey orders?

142
00:15:38.022 --> 00:15:40.061
No excuse. sir.

143
00:15:40.733 --> 00:15:44.777
You're making me look bad.
This is not Dog Company.

144
00:15:44.945 --> 00:15:49.902
This is not Fox Company.
This is Easy Company.

145
00:15:50.074 --> 00:15:54.451
Under my command. this will be
the first and finest company.

146
00:15:56.372 --> 00:15:59.242
I want the names of six men…

147
00:15:59.416 --> 00:16:04.077
their infractions and your
disciplinary recommendations by 0130.

148
00:16:04.254 --> 00:16:05.913
Is that clear?

149
00:16:06.756 --> 00:16:08.879
What infractions. sir?

150
00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:11.673
Find some.

151
00:16:15.639 --> 00:16:17.465
So. what did you do?

152
00:16:17.641 --> 00:16:20.475
Picked six men
and gave them latrine duty.

153
00:16:20.643 --> 00:16:21.806
The lucky six?

154
00:16:21.978 --> 00:16:28.395
McDonald. Toye. Perconte.
Lipton. Muck and Guarnere.

155
00:16:28.567 --> 00:16:31.936
–Why them?
–It was their turn.

156
00:16:32.112 --> 00:16:33.938
Sobel's a genius.

157
00:16:34.114 --> 00:16:37.814
I had a headmaster like him
in school. I know the type.

158
00:16:37.992 --> 00:16:41.824
Lewis. Michelangelo's a genius.
Beethoven's a genius.

159
00:16:41.996 --> 00:16:45.495
You know a man who wouldn't
double-time Currahee…

160
00:16:45.666 --> 00:16:48.750
just to piss in that guy's
morning coffee?

161
00:16:49.377 --> 00:16:50.919
Let's go. let's go.

162
00:16:51.087 --> 00:16:53.459
–Go!
–1000. 2000. 3000. 4000…

163
00:16:53.631 --> 00:16:55.125
Stand in the door.

164
00:16:55.299 --> 00:16:57.126
–Go!
–1000. 2000…

165
00:16:57.301 --> 00:17:00.052
You just broke both your legs. Gordon.

166
00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:03.137
–Are you trying to get killed?
–No. sir!

167
00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:06.382
Stand in the door.

168
00:17:19.779 --> 00:17:21.155
Shit.

169
00:17:27.203 --> 00:17:31.615
To the wall! Over as a team.
Come on. against the wall!

170
00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:34.246
Jesus. what the hell is this?

171
00:17:34.417 --> 00:17:36.659
That's pig guts. boy.

172
00:17:40.256 --> 00:17:42.248
Goddamn it.

173
00:17:44.093 --> 00:17:46.928
–Why are you here?
–To be in the Airborne.

174
00:17:47.095 --> 00:17:50.511
–I don't believe you. Why?
–To be in the Airborne.

175
00:17:50.682 --> 00:17:55.390
You have 50 minutes to the top and
back. and I will be watching you.

176
00:17:55.561 --> 00:17:58.052
What are you waiting for?

177
00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:43.512
Easy Company has the best performance
record in the 2nd Battalion.

178
00:18:43.688 --> 00:18:47.222
I believe every bit of that
is thanks to you.

179
00:18:47.775 --> 00:18:51.558
–Congratulations. Captain Sobel.
–Thank you. sir.

180
00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:56.068
Isn't that Lt Winters leading
Easy Company in PT?

181
00:18:56.241 --> 00:18:57.735
Yes. sir.

182
00:18:57.909 --> 00:19:01.823
He's a good man. I was planning
on giving him these today.

183
00:19:01.996 --> 00:19:06.159
Why don't you do it?
He'd be proud to get them from you.

184
00:19:11.254 --> 00:19:13.626
Pornography. contraband.

185
00:19:17.009 --> 00:19:20.923
Non-regulation clothing. contraband.

186
00:19:21.263 --> 00:19:25.806
This man had 200 prophylactic kits
in his footlocker.

187
00:19:25.975 --> 00:19:30.803
How in the name of God was he gonna
have the strength to fight the war?

188
00:19:31.022 --> 00:19:37.558
How is it Pvt. Tipper has spare time
for so much correspondence?

189
00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:42.197
Captain. are personal letters
to be considered contraband?

190
00:19:43.116 --> 00:19:49.035
These men aren't paratroopers yet.
They have no personal property.

191
00:19:52.082 --> 00:19:53.991
What is this?

192
00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.287
Anybody.

193
00:19:57.087 --> 00:19:58.664
It's a can of peaches.

194
00:19:58.838 --> 00:20:02.788
Lt Nixon thinks this
is a can of peaches.

195
00:20:02.967 --> 00:20:06.336
That is incorrect.
Your weekend pass is cancelled.

196
00:20:06.512 --> 00:20:11.054
This is United States Army property…

197
00:20:11.224 --> 00:20:15.767
which was taken without
authorization from my mess facility.

198
00:20:15.937 --> 00:20:20.682
And I will not tolerate thievery
in my unit. Whose footlocker is this?

199
00:20:20.858 --> 00:20:22.934
Private Parks'. sir.

200
00:20:23.485 --> 00:20:25.525
Get rid of him.

201
00:20:26.738 --> 00:20:31.115
All weekend passes are cancelled.
officers included.

202
00:20:32.535 --> 00:20:34.077
Carry on.

203
00:20:38.248 --> 00:20:39.956
Lt Winters.

204
00:20:47.924 --> 00:20:51.506
Colonel Sink has seen fit
to promote you.

205
00:20:51.677 --> 00:20:55.888
As first lieutenant. you'll serve
as my executive officer.

206
00:20:56.056 --> 00:20:58.760
–Congratulations.
–Thank you. sir.

207
00:20:58.934 --> 00:21:05.185
And as a test of your organizational
skills and command potential…

208
00:21:05.940 --> 00:21:10.815
I am designating you
mess officer for 14 days.

209
00:21:11.153 --> 00:21:13.904
Report to the mess kitchen
at 0515 hours.

210
00:21:14.072 --> 00:21:17.856
Company breakfast
to be served at 0600.

211
00:21:18.034 --> 00:21:19.658
Yes. sir.

212
00:21:20.995 --> 00:21:24.364
And. Dick. there's rain
forecast tomorrow.

213
00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:30.708
The company will have a light afternoon
of lecture and classroom instruction.

214
00:21:31.963 --> 00:21:37.253
A special meal before their afternoon
off would be a welcome change of pace.

215
00:21:37.426 --> 00:21:40.131
–Would you agree?
–Yes. sir.

216
00:21:41.096 --> 00:21:42.923
I like spaghetti.

217
00:21:52.231 --> 00:21:54.224
Hold on. more coming.

218
00:21:54.400 --> 00:21:57.400
These guys are packing it away.

219
00:22:07.703 --> 00:22:11.154
It's orange. Spaghetti ain't
supposed to be orange.

220
00:22:11.332 --> 00:22:14.949
This ain't spaghetti.
It's Army noodles with ketchup.

221
00:22:15.127 --> 00:22:16.751
You ain't gotta eat it.

222
00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:21.498
As an Italian. you know calling
this spaghetti is a mortal sin.

223
00:22:21.674 --> 00:22:23.548
–I'll eat it.
–I'm eating!

224
00:22:23.718 --> 00:22:25.544
Get out of here!

225
00:22:27.179 --> 00:22:29.302
Orders changed! Get up!

226
00:22:29.473 --> 00:22:35.226
Lectures are cancelled! Easy Company
is running up Currahee! Move!

227
00:22:38.064 --> 00:22:41.017
Three miles up. three miles down.

228
00:22:41.525 --> 00:22:44.098
Hi-yo. Silver!

229
00:22:44.403 --> 00:22:46.728
Let's go! Let's go!

230
00:22:50.825 --> 00:22:55.403
You're a washout. Pvt. Hoobler.
You should pack up and go home!

231
00:22:55.579 --> 00:23:01.083
Looks like Gordon's done. Finished?
You do not deserve to get your wings.

232
00:23:01.251 --> 00:23:03.920
Pvt. Randleman. you look tired.

233
00:23:04.087 --> 00:23:07.290
There's an ambulance waiting for you.

234
00:23:07.465 --> 00:23:10.798
It can all be over. right now.
No more pain…

235
00:23:10.968 --> 00:23:14.586
no more Currahee.
no more Captain Sobel.

236
00:23:55.883 --> 00:23:59.715
–Are we ready to be Army paratroopers?
–Yes. sergeant!

237
00:23:59.887 --> 00:24:01.262
I hope so.

238
00:24:01.430 --> 00:24:06.257
This will be the first of five exits
from a C-47 aircraft set for today.

239
00:24:06.434 --> 00:24:08.094
Get ready!

240
00:24:08.770 --> 00:24:11.521
Stand up! Hook up!

241
00:24:11.689 --> 00:24:16.896
Upon completion of your final jump.
you'll be certified paratroopers.

242
00:24:17.069 --> 00:24:18.611
Check equipment!

243
00:24:20.739 --> 00:24:23.360
Sound off for equipment check!

244
00:24:23.533 --> 00:24:25.111
Nine okay!

245
00:24:25.285 --> 00:24:27.989
Eight okay! Seven okay!

246
00:24:28.162 --> 00:24:30.155
Six okay!

247
00:24:30.331 --> 00:24:33.035
Five okay! Four okay!

248
00:24:33.208 --> 00:24:36.292
Three okay! Two okay! One okay!

249
00:24:36.461 --> 00:24:42.048
There'll be many men jumping today.
hopefully under deployed canopies.

250
00:24:42.216 --> 00:24:44.624
Stand in the door!

251
00:24:46.720 --> 00:24:50.967
I guarantee you're gonna love it.
lieutenant! Go! Go!

252
00:24:51.141 --> 00:24:56.562
Jumping from 1000 feet AGL.
in sticks of 12 jumpers per aircraft.

253
00:24:57.355 --> 00:25:00.558
You just have to remember
what you were taught.

254
00:25:00.733 --> 00:25:03.899
I guarantee gravity will
take care of the rest.

255
00:25:04.069 --> 00:25:06.227
Go! Go! Go!

256
00:25:48.275 --> 00:25:49.734
Damn it.

257
00:25:50.903 --> 00:25:56.691
Gentlemen. rest assured. any refusals
in the aircraft or at the door…

258
00:25:57.951 --> 00:26:01.402
and I guarantee you will be
out of the Airborne.

259
00:26:02.496 --> 00:26:06.494
Four okay! Three okay!
Two okay! One okay!

260
00:26:06.667 --> 00:26:08.659
Stand in the door!

261
00:26:10.796 --> 00:26:12.373
Now!

262
00:26:23.390 --> 00:26:26.889
1000. 2000. 3000. 4000. 5000…

263
00:26:27.060 --> 00:26:30.808
6000. 7000. 8000. 9000.

264
00:26:30.980 --> 00:26:32.309
Yeah!

265
00:26:34.483 --> 00:26:36.772
Hi-yo. Silver!

266
00:26:42.240 --> 00:26:46.902
If you had style like me. somebody
might mistake you for somebody.

267
00:26:47.078 --> 00:26:49.995
You mean like your fucking sergeant?

268
00:26:51.040 --> 00:26:53.079
I'm just kidding.

269
00:26:55.419 --> 00:26:57.992
–Congratulations. Martin.
–Cpl Toye.

270
00:26:58.171 --> 00:27:01.587
There will be no leaning
in my company.

271
00:27:02.133 --> 00:27:04.885
Are those dusty jump wings?

272
00:27:05.052 --> 00:27:08.919
How will you slay the Huns
with dust on your jump wings?

273
00:27:09.098 --> 00:27:11.635
Luz. just give me a drink.

274
00:27:13.351 --> 00:27:15.225
Hell of an idea. Joe.

275
00:27:15.395 --> 00:27:17.055
There you go.

276
00:27:18.106 --> 00:27:21.391
Three miles up. three miles down.

277
00:27:22.151 --> 00:27:24.025
Ten-hut!

278
00:27:33.203 --> 00:27:35.907
Well. at ease. paratroopers.

279
00:27:36.956 --> 00:27:40.159
–Good evening. Easy Company.
–Evening. sir!

280
00:27:40.334 --> 00:27:44.283
Parachute Infantry is a new concept
in military history.

281
00:27:44.463 --> 00:27:48.080
But the 506 will forge
that new concept into victory.

282
00:27:48.258 --> 00:27:49.668
Yes. sir!

283
00:27:49.842 --> 00:27:53.543
I want you to know I'm damn proud
of every one of you.

284
00:27:53.721 --> 00:27:56.425
Now. you deserve this party.

285
00:27:56.598 --> 00:27:58.425
–Thanks. Sgt Grant.
–Sir.

286
00:27:58.809 --> 00:28:02.391
So I want you to have fun.
and remember our motto:

287
00:28:02.562 --> 00:28:05.314
–Currahee!
–Currahee!

288
00:28:32.214 --> 00:28:33.708
Petty!

289
00:28:33.882 --> 00:28:35.542
Map! Come on!

290
00:28:36.134 --> 00:28:38.043
Oh. Christ.

291
00:28:50.605 --> 00:28:53.392
We're in the wrong position.

292
00:28:55.443 --> 00:28:59.487
–We're in the wrong position.
–We're in position for ambush.

293
00:28:59.655 --> 00:29:02.655
Let the enemy come
into our killing zone.

294
00:29:02.824 --> 00:29:05.860
They're right out there.
Let's get them.

295
00:29:06.035 --> 00:29:10.780
–Sir. we have perfect cover here.
–Lieutenant. deploy your troops.

296
00:29:12.625 --> 00:29:15.329
2nd Platoon. move out.

297
00:29:15.753 --> 00:29:18.077
–What?
–Tactical column.

298
00:29:37.439 --> 00:29:41.732
You've just been killed.
along with 95% of your company.

299
00:29:41.901 --> 00:29:43.359
Your outfit?

300
00:29:44.153 --> 00:29:46.988
Easy Company.
2nd Battalion. 506.

301
00:29:50.492 --> 00:29:55.734
Leave three wounded men on the ground
and report back to the assembly area.

302
00:29:55.913 --> 00:29:57.787
Goddamn it.

303
00:30:02.503 --> 00:30:04.744
You. You. You.

304
00:30:07.882 --> 00:30:09.542
What are you gonna do?

305
00:30:09.717 --> 00:30:12.884
Nothing. just keep training the men.

306
00:30:13.471 --> 00:30:15.380
Am I interrupting?

307
00:30:16.724 --> 00:30:18.597
No. no.

308
00:30:18.767 --> 00:30:22.764
Lt Lewis Nixon. Lt Harry Welsh.
just in from the 82nd.

309
00:30:22.938 --> 00:30:27.030
–Congratulations on the promotion.
–If you wanna call it that.

310
00:30:27.150 --> 00:30:31.811
You'll learn him pretty quickly.
No flaws. vices or sense of humor.

311
00:30:31.987 --> 00:30:35.403
Just like your chums
up at Battalion Staff?

312
00:30:35.574 --> 00:30:39.108
–What's up?
–I'm hearing a lot of rumblings.

313
00:30:39.285 --> 00:30:42.452
Sobel? We were just
talking about that.

314
00:30:42.622 --> 00:30:45.492
So he gets a little jumpy
in the field.

315
00:30:45.666 --> 00:30:49.366
–He gets jumpy and you get killed.
–That's nice.

316
00:30:49.545 --> 00:30:53.245
Listen. if we discuss it.
it should be among ourselves.

317
00:30:53.423 --> 00:30:55.083
Absolutely.

318
00:31:02.681 --> 00:31:05.386
–2nd Platoon ready?
–Ready. sir.

319
00:31:06.476 --> 00:31:09.762
Then get them in formation.
We're moving out.

320
00:31:09.938 --> 00:31:11.432
Yes. sir.

321
00:31:36.587 --> 00:31:40.798
Goddamn. you gotta admit.
He's got no chance.

322
00:31:40.966 --> 00:31:44.749
Either the Krauts will get him.
or one of us.

323
00:31:44.927 --> 00:31:46.719
Who? Sobel?

324
00:31:46.888 --> 00:31:48.761
He screwed up one maneuver.

325
00:31:48.931 --> 00:31:51.386
I'm always fumbling with grenades.

326
00:31:51.558 --> 00:31:54.559
It would be easy if one
went off by accident.

327
00:31:54.728 --> 00:31:58.428
They must have put him
in charge for a reason.

328
00:31:58.606 --> 00:32:02.354
Because the Army wouldn't
make a mistake. right. Shift?

329
00:32:16.622 --> 00:32:19.374
–Going my way?
–Where the train takes me.

330
00:32:19.542 --> 00:32:21.748
–Where's that?
–I haven't a clue.

331
00:32:21.919 --> 00:32:26.296
Yeah. come on. Take a guess.
Atlantic. Pacific. Atlantic?

332
00:32:26.465 --> 00:32:29.465
I'm not the intelligence officer.

333
00:32:29.884 --> 00:32:33.716
As such. I know. but if I told you.
I'd have to kill you.

334
00:32:33.888 --> 00:32:35.761
So don't tell me.

335
00:32:38.726 --> 00:32:42.557
New York City. Troop ship. England.

336
00:32:45.440 --> 00:32:48.440
We're invading Europe. my friend.

337
00:32:48.609 --> 00:32:50.436
Fortress Europa.

338
00:32:52.113 --> 00:32:54.354
Since when do I drink?

339
00:32:55.782 --> 00:32:59.400
If I thought you'd drink.
I wouldn't offer it to you.

340
00:33:01.204 --> 00:33:04.904
Nix. what are you gonna do
when you get into combat?

341
00:33:07.376 --> 00:33:11.456
Oh. I have every confidence
in my scrounging abilities.

342
00:33:11.630 --> 00:33:16.042
And I have a case of Vat 69
hidden in your footlocker.

343
00:33:19.887 --> 00:33:22.212
–Really?
–Oh. yeah.

344
00:33:23.933 --> 00:33:25.475
Morning.

345
00:33:27.311 --> 00:33:30.395
This could turn into a real nice trip.

346
00:33:46.077 --> 00:33:48.236
Dear Sir or Madam:

347
00:33:48.413 --> 00:33:53.833
Soon your son will drop from the sky
to engage and defeat the enemy.

348
00:33:54.001 --> 00:33:59.671
Your letters of love and encouragement
will arm him with a fighting heart.

349
00:33:59.840 --> 00:34:05.712
With that. he cannot fail but will win
glory for himself. make you proud…

350
00:34:05.887 --> 00:34:10.216
and his country grateful
for his service in its hour of need.

351
00:34:10.391 --> 00:34:14.174
Signed Herbert M Sobel.
Captain. Commanding.

352
00:34:26.906 --> 00:34:31.733
Right now. some lucky bastard's
headed for the South Pacific.

353
00:34:31.910 --> 00:34:34.994
He'll get billeted
on some tropical island.

354
00:34:35.163 --> 00:34:38.329
Sitting under a tree
with naked native girls…

355
00:34:38.499 --> 00:34:42.912
helping him cut up coconuts
so he can hand-feed the flamingos.

356
00:34:43.087 --> 00:34:47.416
–Flamingos are mean. They bite.
–So do the naked native girls.

357
00:34:47.591 --> 00:34:48.871
With any luck.

358
00:34:49.050 --> 00:34:51.422
Guys. I'm glad I'm going to Europe.

359
00:34:51.594 --> 00:34:54.299
Hitler gets this
across the windpipe.

360
00:34:54.472 --> 00:34:57.805
Roosevelt changes Thanksgiving
to Joe Toye Day…

361
00:34:57.975 --> 00:35:01.842
and pays me $10·000 a year
for the rest of my life.

362
00:35:02.020 --> 00:35:05.603
What if they send us to North Africa?

363
00:35:05.774 --> 00:35:09.853
–My brother's there. He says it's hot.
–It's hot in Africa?

364
00:35:10.027 --> 00:35:13.361
Shut up.
Point is. it don't matter where we go.

365
00:35:13.531 --> 00:35:18.607
Once we get into combat. you trust
only yourself and the man next to you.

366
00:35:19.452 --> 00:35:21.908
–Long as he's a paratrooper.
–Yeah?

367
00:35:22.080 --> 00:35:25.246
What if that paratrooper
turns out to be Sobel?

368
00:35:25.416 --> 00:35:28.951
If I'm next to Sobel.
I'm moving down the line.

369
00:35:29.128 --> 00:35:32.828
Hook up with another officer.
like Heyliger or Winters.

370
00:35:33.006 --> 00:35:39.174
I like Winters. But when bullets fly.
I don't want a Quaker fighting for me.

371
00:35:39.345 --> 00:35:42.465
–How do you know that?
–He ain't Catholic.

372
00:35:42.640 --> 00:35:46.933
–Neither's Sobel.
–That prick's a son of Abraham.

373
00:35:47.269 --> 00:35:49.974
–He's what?
–He's a Jew.

374
00:35:50.147 --> 00:35:51.689
Fuck.

375
00:35:53.900 --> 00:35:57.066
–I'm a Jew.
–Congratulations.

376
00:35:57.570 --> 00:36:00.108
Get your nose out of my face.

377
00:36:06.786 --> 00:36:08.660
What's all that about?

378
00:36:08.830 --> 00:36:10.869
Gonorrhea called Sobel a Jew.

379
00:36:11.040 --> 00:36:14.373
Liebgott took offense
because he's a Jew too.

380
00:36:14.919 --> 00:36:18.667
Fighting over Sobel. That's smart.

381
00:36:35.979 --> 00:36:37.687
Attack!

382
00:36:40.859 --> 00:36:43.528
No! You wanna kill him!

383
00:36:43.694 --> 00:36:46.814
Parry right! Parry left!
Front!

384
00:36:46.989 --> 00:36:48.187
Recover.

385
00:36:48.365 --> 00:36:49.563
Okay.

386
00:36:49.742 --> 00:36:55.910
We talked about magnetic declination
and the left-add. right-subtract rule.

387
00:36:56.122 --> 00:36:57.865
Today we'll use it.

388
00:36:58.041 --> 00:37:00.994
There are two basic
fighting positions.

389
00:37:01.168 --> 00:37:03.742
The first is a prepared position.

390
00:37:03.921 --> 00:37:09.507
This position's advantages are that
it gives you cover and concealment.

391
00:37:09.676 --> 00:37:11.834
Commence fire!

392
00:37:15.848 --> 00:37:18.421
We'll maneuver through these trees.

393
00:37:18.684 --> 00:37:23.595
At the same time. our 2nd Platoon.
in this case. moves over here.

394
00:37:23.772 --> 00:37:27.057
He'll then kill or capture
that German.

395
00:37:52.089 --> 00:37:53.797
Sobel's late.

396
00:38:05.809 --> 00:38:08.134
Why is there a fence here?

397
00:38:10.230 --> 00:38:12.851
There should be no fence here.
Tipper!

398
00:38:13.024 --> 00:38:15.230
Give me the map.

399
00:38:17.528 --> 00:38:20.861
Perconte. Luz.
Get the men. Get them ba—

400
00:38:21.031 --> 00:38:26.191
–Take cover behind those trees.
–All right. Let's go. Move it out.

401
00:38:29.456 --> 00:38:32.326
There should—
There should be no fence.

402
00:38:32.500 --> 00:38:34.872
We could go over it. sir.

403
00:38:35.044 --> 00:38:38.495
Really? That's not the point.
Where the goddamn—?

404
00:38:38.672 --> 00:38:41.459
Where the goddamn hell are we?

405
00:38:42.384 --> 00:38:43.546
–Perconte.
–Yeah?

406
00:38:43.718 --> 00:38:46.007
–Sobel's lost again. right?
–Yeah.

407
00:38:46.179 --> 00:38:48.337
–Fucking Christ.
–Hey. Luz?

408
00:38:51.225 --> 00:38:53.930
Can you do Major Horton?

409
00:38:54.103 --> 00:38:57.305
Does a wild bear crap
in the woods. son?

410
00:38:58.065 --> 00:39:01.765
Maybe the major can goose
this schmuck. Get us moving?

411
00:39:01.943 --> 00:39:04.231
–No way. I'm not gonna—
–Oh. yes.

412
00:39:04.404 --> 00:39:06.859
Luz. you gotta. Come on.

413
00:39:07.031 --> 00:39:09.237
All right. just this once.

414
00:39:13.662 --> 00:39:17.991
356833.
Isn't that the intersection?

415
00:39:18.166 --> 00:39:21.499
No. sir. it's here.
You're a full grid off.

416
00:39:21.669 --> 00:39:23.080
Goddamn it.

417
00:39:23.546 --> 00:39:28.705
–Is there a problem. Captain Sobel?
–Who said that? Who broke silence?

418
00:39:28.884 --> 00:39:31.635
I think it's Major Horton. sir.

419
00:39:33.513 --> 00:39:36.763
Major Horton? What. is he—?
Did he join us?

420
00:39:36.933 --> 00:39:39.602
Maybe he's moving
between the platoons.

421
00:39:39.768 --> 00:39:44.430
What is the goddamn holdup.
Mr Sobel⁈

422
00:39:45.732 --> 00:39:49.231
A fence. sir. a—
God!

423
00:39:49.569 --> 00:39:54.111
–A barbed-wire fence.
–Oh. that dog just ain't gonna hunt.

424
00:39:54.323 --> 00:39:55.734
Shut up!

425
00:39:55.908 --> 00:40:00.534
Now. you cut that fence and get this
goddamn platoon on the move!

426
00:40:01.997 --> 00:40:03.788
Yes. sir!

427
00:40:05.875 --> 00:40:08.053
–Where are my wire cutters?
–Sir.

428
00:40:10.254 --> 00:40:14.501
–We have to move.
–Without Sobel and 1st Platoon?

429
00:40:14.675 --> 00:40:17.344
It's a T-intersection. We improvise.

430
00:40:17.511 --> 00:40:21.259
Lay down fire to cut the road
in all directions.

431
00:40:21.639 --> 00:40:26.431
Go right with 1st Squad. Tell 2nd
to go left. I'll be center with 3rd.

432
00:40:26.602 --> 00:40:28.760
–Go.
–Yes. sir.

433
00:40:50.874 --> 00:40:52.581
Dearie me.

434
00:41:03.218 --> 00:41:05.175
Bloody hell.

435
00:41:24.696 --> 00:41:28.645
You've done it now. Yanks.
You've captured me.

436
00:41:32.035 --> 00:41:36.033
Hi-yo. Silver!

437
00:41:38.625 --> 00:41:40.997
Would that be the enemy?

438
00:41:41.169 --> 00:41:43.659
As a matter of fact. yes.

439
00:41:50.969 --> 00:41:54.053
Good work. 2nd Platoon.
We took the objective.

440
00:42:03.188 --> 00:42:06.224
Who was the idiot
who cut that man's fence?

441
00:42:06.399 --> 00:42:08.308
–I was ordered to.
–By who?

442
00:42:08.568 --> 00:42:10.726
–Maj. Horton. sir.
–Maj. Horton?

443
00:42:10.903 --> 00:42:13.192
–Yes.
–He told you to do that?

444
00:42:13.364 --> 00:42:17.313
–Yes. sir.
–He ordered you to cut the fence?

445
00:42:17.493 --> 00:42:19.236
Yes. he did.

446
00:42:19.411 --> 00:42:23.658
Major Horton is on leave in London.

447
00:42:25.625 --> 00:42:28.032
Get those cows out of here.

448
00:42:56.361 --> 00:42:58.187
Lt Winters.

449
00:43:01.115 --> 00:43:04.116
With Capt. Sobel's compliments. sir.

450
00:43:06.453 --> 00:43:07.912
Lieutenant.

451
00:43:26.888 --> 00:43:31.680
–Oh. for crying out loud.
–Misspelled “court-martial”.

452
00:43:36.688 --> 00:43:38.764
No. sir. I do not understand.

453
00:43:38.940 --> 00:43:42.391
Your orders were to inspect
latrines at 1000 hours.

454
00:43:42.569 --> 00:43:48.820
From 0930 to 0955. I was censoring
mail by order of Col. Strayer.

455
00:43:48.991 --> 00:43:51.908
At 1000 hours. I followed your orders.

456
00:43:52.077 --> 00:43:54.782
I changed that time to 0945.

457
00:43:54.955 --> 00:43:57.001
–No one told me.
–I telephoned.

458
00:43:57.165 --> 00:43:59.454
The family I'm with has no phone.

459
00:43:59.626 --> 00:44:02.413
–And sent a runner.
–No runner found me.

460
00:44:02.587 --> 00:44:06.204
When given a task to perform
by a ranking officer…

461
00:44:06.382 --> 00:44:10.924
you should have delegated
latrine inspection to another officer.

462
00:44:11.094 --> 00:44:12.719
You failed to do so.

463
00:44:12.887 --> 00:44:18.676
Were I to let this go unpunished. what
kind of message is that to the men?

464
00:44:18.851 --> 00:44:22.848
–I performed my duty as I was ordered.
–And I disagree.

465
00:44:23.022 --> 00:44:27.066
So your options are
quite simple. lieutenant.

466
00:44:27.234 --> 00:44:31.729
Punishment will be denial
of a 48-hour pass for 60 days.

467
00:44:31.904 --> 00:44:34.739
Stand before me at attention.

468
00:44:37.243 --> 00:44:42.034
Or you may initiate an appeal
and request a trial by court-martial.

469
00:44:46.584 --> 00:44:51.246
You spend weekends on the base anyway.
Be a man. Take the punishment.

470
00:44:51.922 --> 00:44:54.330
May I borrow your pen. sir?

471
00:45:05.810 --> 00:45:07.683
My endorsement. sir.

472
00:45:09.271 --> 00:45:12.058
I request trial by court-martial.

473
00:45:22.616 --> 00:45:25.700
–We lost Winters to the mess.
–You're joking.

474
00:45:25.869 --> 00:45:30.863
Strayer did it while he figures out
the procedures for his court-martial.

475
00:45:31.041 --> 00:45:34.290
–Nixon better get him out.
–And if he don't?

476
00:45:34.460 --> 00:45:38.671
Winters scrambles eggs while
we make the big jump with Sobel.

477
00:45:39.882 --> 00:45:41.340
Not me.

478
00:45:41.967 --> 00:45:46.178
–We're going through with this. right?
–We gotta do something.

479
00:45:46.346 --> 00:45:48.967
–Yeah.
–Yeah.

480
00:45:49.140 --> 00:45:50.468
All right.

481
00:45:51.017 --> 00:45:52.392
Good.

482
00:45:54.103 --> 00:45:59.263
–Let's be clear of the consequences.
–I don't care about the consequences.

483
00:45:59.691 --> 00:46:03.107
We could be lined up
against a wall and shot.

484
00:46:04.487 --> 00:46:06.978
Now. I'm ready to face that.

485
00:46:08.032 --> 00:46:11.033
And every one of us had better be too.

486
00:46:15.872 --> 00:46:19.739
I will not follow that man
into combat.

487
00:46:22.670 --> 00:46:24.330
Me neither.

488
00:46:26.757 --> 00:46:28.168
All right.

489
00:46:29.510 --> 00:46:31.467
Then let's do it.

490
00:46:44.857 --> 00:46:46.814
“I hereby…

491
00:46:48.110 --> 00:46:50.102
”no longer…

492
00:46:51.237 --> 00:46:53.230
”wish to serve…

493
00:46:55.408 --> 00:46:57.945
”as a non-commissioned officer…

494
00:47:04.499 --> 00:47:06.456
in Easy Company.”

495
00:47:20.096 --> 00:47:23.299
All right. boys. Good luck.

496
00:47:28.229 --> 00:47:30.766
I ought to have you all shot!

497
00:47:30.939 --> 00:47:35.850
This is an act of mutiny while
we prepare for the invasion of Europe.

498
00:47:36.027 --> 00:47:38.150
–Sgt Harris?
–Sir.

499
00:47:38.321 --> 00:47:39.863
Turn in your stripes.

500
00:47:40.323 --> 00:47:43.193
You are transferred
out of my regiment.

501
00:47:43.451 --> 00:47:45.443
–Sir.
–Get out.

502
00:47:46.829 --> 00:47:49.154
–Sgt Ranney?
–Sir.

503
00:47:49.331 --> 00:47:52.581
You're lucky I'm only
busting you to private.

504
00:47:52.751 --> 00:47:56.202
All of you NCOs have disgraced
the 101st Airborne.

505
00:47:56.712 --> 00:48:01.421
You're lucky we're on the eve of
the largest action in war history…

506
00:48:01.592 --> 00:48:06.799
which leaves me no choice
but to spare your lives.

507
00:48:08.973 --> 00:48:12.307
Now. get out of my office
and out of my sight.

508
00:48:12.477 --> 00:48:13.805
Get.

509
00:48:30.159 --> 00:48:33.160
Keep them coming. Thattaboy.
That's it.

510
00:49:05.691 --> 00:49:09.225
I can only speculate.
Most men would never do this.

511
00:49:09.402 --> 00:49:13.400
But I believe just a few
of the sergeants may have felt…

512
00:49:13.573 --> 00:49:17.902
their loyalty lay more
to the platoon than to the company.

513
00:49:18.369 --> 00:49:22.829
And these few convinced the other
NCOs to turn in their stripes?

514
00:49:22.998 --> 00:49:26.248
As staff sergeants.
they have a great influence.

515
00:49:26.418 --> 00:49:30.249
But the rest are good men.
I can work with them.

516
00:49:36.802 --> 00:49:41.345
Winters' court-martial has been
an unpleasant distraction.

517
00:49:41.514 --> 00:49:43.839
Indeed it has. sir.

518
00:49:44.142 --> 00:49:48.934
However. your command of Easy
Company has been exemplary.

519
00:49:49.105 --> 00:49:50.764
Thank you. sir.

520
00:49:51.482 --> 00:49:56.439
In fact. except for the actions
of a few of your non-coms…

521
00:49:56.611 --> 00:50:01.072
you fielded one of the finest
companies of soldiers I've seen.

522
00:50:01.240 --> 00:50:02.734
Yes. sir.

523
00:50:03.743 --> 00:50:08.618
Division has established a parachute
training school at Chilton Foliat.

524
00:50:08.789 --> 00:50:12.833
The idea is for non-infantry types…

525
00:50:13.001 --> 00:50:16.915
vital to the invasion.
such as doctors and chaplains…

526
00:50:17.088 --> 00:50:19.709
to take jump training there.

527
00:50:20.383 --> 00:50:25.589
I can't think of anyone more qualified
to command such a school than you.

528
00:50:28.431 --> 00:50:29.807
Sir?

529
00:50:33.186 --> 00:50:36.352
I'm reassigning you to Chilton Foliat.

530
00:50:44.738 --> 00:50:46.730
I'm losing Easy Company?

531
00:50:46.906 --> 00:50:49.990
The war effort needs you elsewhere.

532
00:50:55.789 --> 00:50:59.039
–Permission to speak. sir.
–Granted.

533
00:51:03.129 --> 00:51:05.798
Is—? Who will be replacing me?

534
00:51:05.965 --> 00:51:09.796
Lt Meehan from Baker Company
is senior.

535
00:51:11.637 --> 00:51:15.883
Good luck at Chilton Foliat. Herbert.
Don't let us down. now.

536
00:51:22.229 --> 00:51:23.688
No. sir.

537
00:51:30.570 --> 00:51:32.230
Carry on.

538
00:52:25.453 --> 00:52:30.612
2nd Platoon. listen up. I want
the 1st Squad in A-side tents there.

539
00:52:30.791 --> 00:52:33.460
3rd Squad. second row…

540
00:52:47.431 --> 00:52:49.470
Holy shit!

541
00:52:50.725 --> 00:52:53.845
No. it's all right.
We're Tommies. not Boche.

542
00:52:54.020 --> 00:52:56.261
–Is all this real?
–Yeah. yeah.

543
00:52:56.439 --> 00:53:01.895
It's for you lads. so you can get your
mince pies on some Jerry clobber.

544
00:53:02.069 --> 00:53:04.904
–If you know what I mean.
–Not really.

545
00:53:05.071 --> 00:53:06.447
You got a Luger?

546
00:53:06.614 --> 00:53:10.398
–I'm dying to hold a real Luger.
–Yeah. go on. then.

547
00:53:11.577 --> 00:53:13.866
Quick butchers. yeah?

548
00:53:17.416 --> 00:53:20.251
–She's a doozy.
–That's pukka. isn't it?

549
00:53:20.627 --> 00:53:22.370
–What?
–Eh?

550
00:53:23.213 --> 00:53:24.872
Hey. Petty!

551
00:53:25.048 --> 00:53:26.672
Hey. mate?

552
00:53:28.092 --> 00:53:31.986
You're having a bath if you think
you're half-inching that.

553
00:53:32.137 --> 00:53:34.628
Oh. yeah. Sorry. Well. good luck.

554
00:53:34.806 --> 00:53:36.431
You too. mate.

555
00:53:37.684 --> 00:53:39.059
What's up. Hoobs?

556
00:53:40.103 --> 00:53:43.934
These men have been through
the Army's toughest training.

557
00:53:44.106 --> 00:53:48.732
Under the worst circumstances.
And they volunteered for it.

558
00:53:48.902 --> 00:53:51.475
I was just shooting craps with them—

559
00:53:51.655 --> 00:53:53.694
You know why they volunteered?

560
00:53:53.865 --> 00:53:59.203
So when things got bad. the man
next to them would be the best.

561
00:53:59.370 --> 00:54:04.364
–Not a draftee who'll get them killed.
–Are you mad because they like me?

562
00:54:04.541 --> 00:54:07.411
Because I'm getting
to know my soldiers?

563
00:54:07.586 --> 00:54:12.745
You've been with these guys two years?
I've been here for six days.

564
00:54:12.924 --> 00:54:16.008
–You were gambling.
–So? Soldiers do that.

565
00:54:16.177 --> 00:54:20.340
–I don't deserve a reprimand for it.
–What if you'd won?

566
00:54:21.890 --> 00:54:25.389
–What?
–What if you'd won?

567
00:54:30.106 --> 00:54:34.648
Never put yourself in a position
where you can take from these men.

568
00:54:39.322 --> 00:54:41.398
–Lt Meehan?
–Enter.

569
00:54:43.910 --> 00:54:47.528
On the last training jump…
I had a compass.

570
00:54:48.706 --> 00:54:50.579
Close the flap.

571
00:54:52.501 --> 00:54:54.410
–Then we turned left.
–Yeah.

572
00:54:54.586 --> 00:54:58.535
Bearing 0-4-2.12 minutes.

573
00:54:58.715 --> 00:55:01.336
–Then another left.
–Yes.

574
00:55:01.509 --> 00:55:04.046
Call it 3-5-8.

575
00:55:05.095 --> 00:55:07.301
For 10½ minutes.

576
00:55:07.723 --> 00:55:11.138
–Green light. right over Ramsbury.
–Ramsbury.

577
00:55:11.309 --> 00:55:13.218
Every single time.

578
00:55:13.978 --> 00:55:18.058
Linear distance on the grid
of about…

579
00:55:20.067 --> 00:55:22.273
Okay. Ramsbury.

580
00:55:23.528 --> 00:55:25.070
Upottery.

581
00:55:32.620 --> 00:55:34.031
So…

582
00:55:34.580 --> 00:55:36.537
It's Normandy.

583
00:55:37.332 --> 00:55:40.167
Sainte-Marie-du-Mont.
Causeway number one.

584
00:55:40.335 --> 00:55:44.415
Causeway number two.
The ultimate field problem.

585
00:55:45.131 --> 00:55:50.006
The Douve River estuary divides two
beachheads. code name Utah. here…

586
00:55:50.177 --> 00:55:52.134
and Omaha. here.

587
00:55:52.304 --> 00:55:57.215
Seaborne Infantry will hit these
beaches at a specified date and time.

588
00:55:57.892 --> 00:55:59.932
H-Hour. D-Day.

589
00:56:00.103 --> 00:56:04.147
Airborne's objective is to take
the town of Carentan…

590
00:56:04.315 --> 00:56:08.182
linking Utah and Omaha
into a continuous beachhead.

591
00:56:08.360 --> 00:56:12.192
—linking Omaha and Utah
into one continuous beachhead.

592
00:56:12.489 --> 00:56:18.692
Each trooper will learn this operation
and know his mission to the detail.

593
00:56:18.870 --> 00:56:20.743
–Lt Meehan?
–Yes. Dukeman.

594
00:56:20.913 --> 00:56:24.163
–Are we dropping tonight?
–We'll let you know.

595
00:56:24.333 --> 00:56:28.911
In the meantime. study these
sand tables. maps and recon photos…

596
00:56:29.087 --> 00:56:31.874
until you can draw a map by memory.

597
00:56:32.048 --> 00:56:34.669
We'll drop behind
this Atlantic Wall…

598
00:56:34.884 --> 00:56:38.466
five hours before the 4th Infantry
lands at Utah.

599
00:56:38.846 --> 00:56:43.922
Between our assembly area and the
objective. there is a German garrison.

600
00:56:44.100 --> 00:56:46.674
In this area. Sainte-Marie-du-Mont.

601
00:56:46.853 --> 00:56:50.387
Easy Company
will destroy that garrison.

602
00:56:52.566 --> 00:56:56.979
Three-day supply of K rations.
chocolate bars. powdered coffee…

603
00:56:57.154 --> 00:57:01.103
sugar. matches. compass.
bayonet. ammunition…

604
00:57:01.282 --> 00:57:06.442
gas mask. musette bag with ammo.
my webbing. my .45. canteen…

605
00:57:06.621 --> 00:57:11.163
cartons of smokes. Hawkins mine.
smoke grenade. Gammon grenade…

606
00:57:11.333 --> 00:57:14.832
TNT. this bullshit
and a pair of nasty skivvies.

607
00:57:15.003 --> 00:57:16.118
Your point?

608
00:57:16.296 --> 00:57:20.982
This weighs as much as I do. I still
got my chute. my Mae West and M-1.

609
00:57:21.092 --> 00:57:25.041
–Where are your brass knuckles?
–I could use some.

610
00:57:25.221 --> 00:57:27.758
–Sgt Martin!
–Vest. anything for me?

611
00:57:27.931 --> 00:57:30.303
Nope. Sgt Martin!

612
00:57:37.815 --> 00:57:39.226
Talbert!

613
00:57:39.400 --> 00:57:41.938
Floyd. Floyd M
Here.

614
00:57:42.611 --> 00:57:45.814
–Heavy. Condoms?
–I don't know. probably.

615
00:57:45.989 --> 00:57:49.856
–What you got?
–“Dear Floyd: Give them hell.”

616
00:57:50.034 --> 00:57:53.652
It's from chief of the Kokomo
Police Department.

617
00:57:57.041 --> 00:57:58.914
You gotta love cops.

618
00:57:59.084 --> 00:58:01.753
All right. listen up! Listen up!

619
00:58:01.920 --> 00:58:06.131
If you did not sign your
GI life insurance policy…

620
00:58:06.299 --> 00:58:11.637
you go on and see Sgt Evans
at the Headquarters Company tent.

621
00:58:11.804 --> 00:58:16.264
You boys don't let your families
miss out on $10·000.

622
00:58:16.433 --> 00:58:18.176
–You hear. Gerry?
–Lip!

623
00:58:18.351 --> 00:58:19.810
Yeah. boy?

624
00:58:22.438 --> 00:58:25.474
–Has Guarnere mentioned his brother?
–No.

625
00:58:25.649 --> 00:58:27.227
I got a problem.

626
00:58:27.401 --> 00:58:31.944
My wife keeps up with things at home.
Casualty lists and like that.

627
00:58:32.114 --> 00:58:35.067
–Guarnere's brother in Italy…
–Henry?

628
00:58:35.241 --> 00:58:37.815
Killed in Monte Cassino.

629
00:58:38.661 --> 00:58:43.868
–Well. I'm sure he doesn't know.
–Damn. What do you think I should do?

630
00:58:44.208 --> 00:58:50.210
–If it were me? I'd tell him.
–A couple hours before we jump?

631
00:58:50.422 --> 00:58:51.536
I don't know.

632
00:59:01.223 --> 00:59:04.259
Why are they springing these
on us now?

633
00:59:04.434 --> 00:59:07.601
It's just 80 extra pounds
strapped to your leg.

634
00:59:07.770 --> 00:59:11.221
Does anybody have any idea
how this thing works?

635
00:59:12.066 --> 00:59:13.560
Colonel Sink.

636
00:59:16.361 --> 00:59:17.856
Colonel Sink.

637
00:59:19.906 --> 00:59:21.982
“Soldiers of the regiment:

638
00:59:22.158 --> 00:59:25.492
”Tonight is the night…

639
00:59:25.661 --> 00:59:27.321
”of nights.

640
00:59:28.080 --> 00:59:31.947
”As you read this. you are en route
to the adventure…

641
00:59:32.126 --> 00:59:35.494
for which you have trained
for over two years.”

642
00:59:36.588 --> 00:59:39.339
That's why they gave us ice cream.

643
00:59:41.467 --> 00:59:44.421
Easy Company! Listen up!

644
00:59:46.347 --> 00:59:49.383
Channel coast is socked in
with rain and fog.

645
00:59:49.558 --> 00:59:51.799
No jump tonight.

646
00:59:52.435 --> 00:59:58.307
The invasion has been postponed.
We're on a 24-hour stand-down.

647
01:00:29.886 --> 01:00:31.842
“Dearest Johnny?”

648
01:00:37.309 --> 01:00:40.144
I got the wrong goddamn jacket.

649
01:00:53.949 --> 01:00:56.071
“Bill Guarnere's brother…”

650
01:02:29.826 --> 01:02:32.531
–Good luck. lads.
–See you. Tommy.

651
01:02:32.704 --> 01:02:34.577
Give Jerry one for me.

652
01:02:54.431 --> 01:02:55.973
Johnny.

653
01:03:02.147 --> 01:03:04.472
You might be looking for this.

654
01:03:04.649 --> 01:03:07.733
I took your jacket by mistake.
I'm sorry.

655
01:03:07.902 --> 01:03:09.479
You read it?

656
01:03:11.447 --> 01:03:16.441
–Where the fuck is Monte Cassino?
–I don't know. Italy somewhere.

657
01:03:19.203 --> 01:03:21.825
Sorry about your brother. Bill.

658
01:03:21.998 --> 01:03:24.405
I'm sorry for my ma.

659
01:03:24.750 --> 01:03:26.493
He was…

660
01:03:30.672 --> 01:03:32.415
Let's get this over with.

661
01:03:36.385 --> 01:03:37.465
Bill?

662
01:03:40.639 --> 01:03:43.260
I'll meet up with you over there.

663
01:03:46.853 --> 01:03:49.807
Doc Roe is giving these out
for airsickness.

664
01:03:49.981 --> 01:03:55.022
Orders are. every man takes one now.
Another. 30 minutes in the air.

665
01:03:55.528 --> 01:03:56.938
Lieutenant.

666
01:04:03.410 --> 01:04:05.900
2nd Platoon. listen up.

667
01:04:08.664 --> 01:04:10.158
Good luck.

668
01:04:11.500 --> 01:04:13.291
God bless you.

669
01:04:14.837 --> 01:04:17.837
I'll see you in the assembly area.

670
01:05:11.721 --> 01:05:16.548
If the wire cuts are successful.
all we should have to deal with is…

671
01:05:21.396 --> 01:05:25.725
–Goddamn. Lieb.
–That airsick pill is making me loopy.

672
09:00:00.000 --> 09:00:01.000
⬄24000÷1001⬄

672
